<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			12/6/97		   5/6/97	     14/6/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	425-450			475	     350-375</p>
<p>    Naphtha	  75-100		  100-125		 50-75</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,900		    1,700		 1,400</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	275-300		  400-425	     300-325</p>
<p>    Jet kero	  15-20		    10-15		  5-10</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks dipped as cargoes moved to other NWE ports. Barge movements were broadly balanced.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks fell as no cargoes arrived, but product left by barge to the German chemical sector.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks rose with cargo arrivals from Russia and the Mediterranean. Some barges left down the Rhine and to Benelux.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks fell as cargoes took material elsewhere in NWE and no new product arrived. Some vacuum gas oil departed for Germany.</p>
<p>Jet fuel inventories were slightly higher.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
